# Line endings: the repository stores LF, and every checkout gets LF, whatever
# the git's own core.autocrlf says. Without this, Windows git with
# autocrlf=true checks out CRLF, MSYS2's git (another home, no autocrlf) then
# reports every such file as modified, and files rewritten by tools come out
# LF, so a working tree ends up mixed. eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# never converted, never diffed as text (a gzipped .xmpuzzle is found binary
# by text=auto; some test files are plain XML)
*.png      binary
*.ico      binary
*.icns     binary
